toD1 sends an element of D₀ to the element of D₁ whose neighbourhoods are the XPseq sets for which the matching set of the first enumeration belongs to the given element. A neighbourhood of the image lies in D₁ because XPseq sets are neighbourhoods. The master is the image of the zero index once the zero convention identifies XPseq at zero with the master. An intersection is the XPseq set at the index supplied by the intersection lemma on the first side. For an upward step, the covering names the larger neighbourhood as a set of the second enumeration, the cross-order transfer turns the inclusion into an inclusion of a first-enumeration set in a YPseq set, upward closure in the original element and the first covering produce an index, and the equality transfer certifies that the larger neighbourhood is the XPseq set at that index.
